<urn:atm:triage:finding/AV3-B3>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AV3-B3" ;
  triage:title "Scanner primitives admit silent false negatives in merge-gate position" ;
  triage:description "(a) extract_fn_body (boundary_enforcement.rs:3815) counts raw braces with no comment/string-literal exclusion — a `}` inside a comment or string truncates the scanned region so a real spawn_blocking after it silently escapes; the same file already strips `//` comments in contains_adapter_availability_inference and uses syn visitors for identical tasks. (b) function_names (:3796) picks up names from comment text (spurious panic) and silently drops generic fns (`fn foo<T>(` fails the alnum filter). (c) the D1 enumerator (:3771) recognises only ControlPathSyncBridge::run( or .run( via a self.<field> declared literally `: ControlPathSyncBridge`; an inline-constructed bridge (`let b = ControlPathSyncBridge::new(pool); b.run(...)`) is invisible to both branches so assert_eq!(sites, RESIDUAL) still passes, defeating D1's 'any new call site fails' guarantee. Fix-shaping: settle syn-AST vs hardened-string scanning once; that remediates B3(a)(b)(c) plus M1, M2, M3. Reviewer ids RBP-AV3-1 (critical), RBP-AV3-2, RBQA-AV3-002." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-av" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-31T06:19:51Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-30T22:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AV3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-31T05:33:39Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
